  "figure_captions": {
    "fig01_candidate_mean_bound.png": "Figure 1. Mean calibrated physical error bound for every candidate and transfer protocol. Targets are shown in separate panels because their units differ.",
    "fig02_candidate_row_coverage.png": "Figure 2. Observation-level coverage of each candidate's physical q90 upper bound. The dashed 0.90 line is the frozen marginal target.",
    "fig03_candidate_group_coverage.png": "Figure 3. Fraction of complete cruises whose within-cruise 90th-percentile absolute error is covered. Cruises, rather than dense rows, are the evidence units.",
    "fig04_selected_fold_coverage.png": "Figure 4. Fold-specific row coverage for the selected estimator in each protocol. No fold is removed when it performs worse than the pooled result.",
    "fig05_sss_reliability.png": "Figure 5. SSS observed 90th-percentile absolute error versus the mean calibrated upper bound in each predicted-bound decile. Points below the diagonal are conservative.",
    "fig06_fco2_reliability.png": "Figure 6. fCO2 observed 90th-percentile absolute error versus the mean calibrated upper bound in each predicted-bound decile. Points below the diagonal are conservative.",
    "fig07_region_coverage.png": "Figure 7. Distribution of row coverage across adequately sampled ocean-region by protocol cohorts. Cohorts below 0.85 are retained as failed evidence rather than hidden by pooling.",
    "fig08_support_coverage.png": "Figure 8. Distribution of coverage across adequately sampled fixed geographic, environmental, cruise-diversity, and temporal-support strata. Failed strata require VF or U in later product mapping."
  },
